{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1563125-giving-permanence-to-ephemeral-objects","id":1563125,"title":"Giving permanence to ephemeral objects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-15T08:55:37-07:00","id":1563125,"title":"Giving permanence to ephemeral objects","content":"As per topic.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for a mechanism or Rote to transport ephemeral items from an umbral realm into the Material and make them stick. If there is one RAW I haven't found it, and would be grateful for a pointer to where it may hide.<br /> <br /> AFAIK anything ephemeral taken from a realm into the Material will only last a short while and then start to fade. <i>Technically</i> all ephemera are Spirits, but I'm not looking for a way to make animate Spirits permanent residents of the Material - actually, I think that should be a separate process and require a lot more oomph.<br /> <br /> I'm also not overly concerned with the transfer of the item for now, as I think it makes sense to look at that as a separate process, too.<br /> <br /> I have a few possible ideas:<br /> <br /> <b>1. Spell:</b> I would clock this as a Spirit 2 + Prime 2 effect.<br /> This would be imo ok for minor items. Get a bottle of liquid Pathos from the Shadowlands, or a minor Device from the Cyber Realm. Difficult to say where to draw the line - would more exotic properties be more vulgar? Would the transfer rob the item of its properties because it's now in a different reality context?<br /> <br /> <b>2. Consecration:</b> Just as you can make material items persist in the umbra, couldn't you bind ephemeral items to make them stick? Or is that too cheap?<br /> <br /> <b>3. Wonders/Trinkets:</b> You could count transferred items as Wonders, and use those rules (sans crafting process). Ups the difficulty of the process considerably, but could preserve more outlandish properties.<br /> <br /> Any help or thoughts on this are welcome. There's a difficulty in balancing the effect, as well as complications and exploits depending on the nature (and source) of the item. Dreaming up Excalibur and taking it out from there should be theoretically possible, but locked behind reasonable difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T18:43:13-07:00","id":1563131,"title":"","content":"Spirit directly states what you need to &quot;imbue objects with Ephemeral power&quot; (Spirit 2 + Matter 2), transmute matter into Ephemera (Spirit 3), craft objects out of Ephemera (Spirit 3 + Matter 3 + Prime 2), Bind spirits into Fetishes (Spirit 4), rend the Gauntlet (Spirit 4) and attain complete control (Spirit 5). So we have options.<br /> <br /> But first I'll be blunt: to make an Ephemeral object stay <i>indefinitely</i> in the Material is Spirit 5. No other Sphere and no way around it. Any other Magic to do it will be subject to duration as per the Sphere, it's also very clear about it.<br /> <br /> Adding stuff can make your creation different in many ways, but won't make it Lasting.<br /> <br /> That aside, first study the object you want to bring. Not every ephemeral object is the same within the Material, some items will remain just from being brought, whatever the means.<br /> <br /> If you want the properties of an item, but not the specific item, Spirit 2 + Matter 2 should be enough at least for &quot;physical properties&quot;. Take the ephemeral object, a mundane replica, and transfer the properties from one to the other. I don't think it will carry Charms or some other powers, but whatever is &quot;natural&quot; to the item in its home realm should be transferred.<br /> <br /> Prime will help with a few odd cases, but don't rely on it too much. Mostly it will help when the item violates conservation laws too blatantly, like a gun with infinite ammo. But Blessing or Perfecting are things Prime does just for being Prime and won't work differently on Ephemera. The &quot;magical&quot; properties of such items are something else.<br /> <br /> Transmute Ephemera into matter or prolonging its stay upon arriving in the Material should be Spirit 3, maybe with Matter 3. It's the same as crafting an object out of Ephemera, but you're getting one that already exists. This is also just the reverse of Stepping Sideways, so shouldn't be harder. That would be your basic answer, and I'd say Prime 2 here is kind of Sphere Bloat more than anything.<br /> <br /> What I'd say Matter and Prime add to Spirit 3 in this regard is control over the result. With only Spirit 3 you're stuck with whatever happens to the object in the transition, which may include it being intangible or having properties change as you guessed. Add Matter 3 and you control what it's made of, so you can ensure it is solid and has the material properties of had before (even if it isn't a material that exists in reality, you're not creating it, the object is already that even if in ephemeral form). Prime 2 should be enough to make most special properties and Charms transfer seamlessly instead of getting butchered by reality (or change unpredictably).<br /> <br /> Normal rules for Fetishes aside, with Spirit 4 you can try to use an ephemeral object as the spirit. I'd probably let it fly and mostly result in a physical object that can use the properties of the ephemeral item within. But that'll probably awaken the item, or awaken something, so while it would be potentially Lasting-like, it's as unpredictable as any Fetishe.<br /> <br /> You can also rend the Gauntlet with Spirit 4 to bring the item, which may or may not have the same effects as bringing through the Gauntlet, or may have more interesting results.<br /> <br /> Finally, yeah, Spirit 5 and you just do it.<br /> <br /> Now, Vulgarity is a tricky question, because the item itself is <i>not</i> subject to it. Fetishes are sought out by many Mages precisely because the lack of Paradox compensates their less predictable nature. So I'd say most methods wouldn't be affected by the item's properties, only by how they came. The lower Spirit 2 + Matter 2 would be the only exception.<br /> <br /> Everything here bypasses most limits to get an item of power because the two things you said to be a different process are, in fact, a different process and way harder than normal.<br /> <br /> Just because you imagined an item it doesn't means its spiritual version exists, is exactly like you thought, you know where in the multiverse it is, it is in a close by realm or you can reach it with a spell. If you use crossover rules it will probably be Glamour and dissolve into nothing due to Banality anyway.<br /> <br /> Overall you're not talking about an alternative way to get magical items. You're talking ways of bringing an item that may already have given you quite the trouble to get in the first place. And that includes things like harvesting Plasm in the Underworld and stuff, which should be in the easier side of all that spectrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T04:26:52-07:00","id":1563140,"title":"","content":"I think I need some concrete examples to see if I got all that correctly.<br /> <br /> <b>Anything with no special properties, but unique identity.</b><br /> Spirit 2 + Matter 2<br /> A Rembrandt painting, destroyed but remembered (Relic).<br /> Water from the River of Death.<br /> A grimoire from an astral library.<br /> <br /> <b>Materials with unique properties.</b><br /> Spirit 3 (+ Prime 2) (+ Matter 3)<br /> Plasm, liquid Pathos, powdered Angst.<br /> Ephemeral Tass or Dross.<br /> <br /> <b>Items with properties that exceed their native material properties.</b><br /> Spirit 4 (Fetish) or Prime 4 (Device)<br /> A fishing net that can catch plasmics (Artifact).<br /> Anti-gravity Device.<br /> <br /> Spirit 5 to manifest something <b>permanently </b>with all properties intact.<br /> <br /> If you have players go on umbral quests, they will inevitably want to keep some of the things they encounter, either as a memento or for utility. Especially for mementos or simple utility items, it seems a bit unfair to take those away later because they fade away. Spirit 5 is a pretty tall order.<br /> As you have guessed, I'm also having an eye on 'economy' here. You can recreate exotic materials with Matter 5, or craft a Wonder with the desired effects- the question is whether getting the item from umbral realms is worth it. I think for trophies of quests and unique items like the first category it may be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1563125-giving-permanence-to-ephemeral-objects?p=1563131#post1563131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That aside, first study the object you want to bring. Not every ephemeral object is the same within the Material, some items will remain just from being brought, whatever the means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I ask, where did you get this from? Looking up exceptions would be interesting, if there is such a list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1563125-giving-permanence-to-ephemeral-objects?p=1563131#post1563131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that'll probably awaken the item, or awaken something, so while it would be potentially Lasting-like, it's as unpredictable as any Fetishe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Waking the Spirit presents an interesting alternative of access. You could summon the object when needed and let it remain in its astral pocket. Of course, a free Spirit may roam or be otherwise unwilling to cooperate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T18:03:01-07:00","id":1563149,"title":"","content":"Right, let's go from highest priority to lowest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Natural permanence</b></u><br /> <br /> That's an extrapolation from the variety of Realms found in the <i>Umbrae</i>. Realms diverge in physics and metaphysics to an astounding degree, including many where things work very similar to the <i>Material</i>, to the point that some or all denizens have full material stats.<br /> <br /> We don't really know what <b>Ephemera</b> is, and if it is really a single substance or class, or just the way otherworldly substances interact with the natives of the <i>Material</i>. When it comes to each <i>Realm</i> nothing is universal. Usual rules apply to &quot;the spaces between&quot; that we call <i>High</i>, <i>Middle</i> and <i>Low Umbrae. </i>Enter a <i>Realm</i> and everything is up in the air.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bottom line</b></u>, feel free to have some objects be more or less stable in the <i>Material</i>. If an object makes sense becoming stable, let it be stable and the PCs figure out why. If it will make for a better story, have a normally unstable object be stable. <i>Realms</i> should play a role, their objects being harder or easier to stabilize.<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>EXAMPLE</b></u></i><br /> <br /> In a journey to the <i>Spires</i>, the cabal find a city of the <b>Djinni</b> abandoned long ago. They explore, face some old spells gone out of control, and get their hands in some exquisite ancient swords with Damascus steel patterns and each capable of slicing one particular material that should be impossible.<br /> <br /> Upon return most of them will start to dissolve after a time, the PCs trying to study what they can while it lasts. After a month, though, one of the swords is still there and gives no sign of dematerializing. It can still cut any silver alloy as if it was mixed with butter instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Spirit 2 \u2013 Touch Spirit</b></u><br /> <br /> If you just want the players to have something from their journey, this is your staple. Objects made of <b>Ephemera</b> rarely can survive for long in the <i>Material</i> before dissipating. But they can and do stay in the <i>Penumbra</i> just fine, adjacent to the <i>Material</i>. And for a <b>Mage</b> with <b><u>Spirit 2</u></b> this is almost a mere technicality.<br /> <br /> An <b>Ephemeral</b> object in the <i>Penumbra</i> won't leave its position unless taken by something, and with <u><b>Spirit 2</b></u> the <b>Mage</b> can reach the place with any sense and touch, so the object is still spatially nearby and the character can interact with little effort. The downside is that creative effects are necessary if you want to use it in other <i>Material</i> things, but the pros are both that the item is usually safer against robbery in the <i>Penumbra</i> and that interacting with it is most certainly <b>Coincidental</b> (if weird).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bottom line</b></u>, a <b>Mage</b> with <u><b>Spirit 2</b></u> can basically treat the <i>Penumbra</i> as an extension of their immediate vicinity and their home. The object is already in their hands, only limited in touch of material things.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>EXAMPLE</b></i></u><br /> <br /> The cabal doesn't take chances with all those swords. After a few tests in the <i>Material</i> they take the weapons back into the <i>Penumbra</i>. The <u><b>Spirit</b></u> <b>Mage</b> can help everyone in the <b>Sanctum</b> to see and study things in the <i>Penumbra</i>, and once they're finished the swords rest in their Trophy Room, even if at the <i>Other Side</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Spirit 2 + Matter 2 \u2013 Infuse with Ephemeral Properties</b></u><br /> <br /> You got this one wrong, you're not bringing any item with you. But you're bringing their unusual properties, or a close semblance of them. With <u><b>Matter 2</b></u> you can imbue a physical object with <b>Touch Spirit</b>, for it to interact with things in the <i>Penumbra</i>. More importantly, you can imbue it with the properties of <b>Ephemera</b>.<br /> <br /> Usually that just means the object will be able to touch anything there, but with an ephemeral object at hand you can use this particular item as the template for the effect, more effective if the material object is similar to the ephemeral one.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bottom line</b></u>, you'll take a lookalike of the item brought from the <i>Umbra</i>, <b>Magically</b> silver tape the two of them across the <i>Gauntlet</i>, then use <u><b>Spirit + Matter</b></u> to turn the material replica into an exact mirror that copies the otherworldly material.<br /> <br /> It's a temporary effect, but ending just means you have to make it again, as both items are in their respective realities anyway, so nothing else changes for them.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>EXAMPLE</b></i></u><br /> <br /> The ancient <b>Djinn</b> swords are like 17th century sabers. Not precisely, but close enough. The <b>Mage</b> buy a good replica from a trusted artisan and uses <b>Magic</b> to impose the reality of the old genie sword upon the replica.<br /> <br /> Slowly the new sword changes appearance to match the exquisite material and pattern in the blade. This transmutation is <b>Vulgar</b>, but the resulting sword likely isn't, despite being made of the strange alloy of the genies.<br /> <br /> But this effect is somewhat unpredictable. The physical sword is now made of the same material as the original, but in a non ephemeral version it's impossible to say how much it will work as it did in the <i>Umbra</i>. It can also touch the <i>Penumbra</i> as if it was in both sides. It's up to the <b>ST</b> which properties will transfer, which will not and which will appear that neither had before. If the swords are enchanted on top of being made of otherworldly substances, those enchantments won't be copied.<br /> <br /> You can't take the Rembrandt or the grimoire with that, as the material they're made of is not what makes them valuable and <u><b>Matter 2</b></u> only changes composition, not form. But the water of the <b>River of Death</b>, <b>Plasm</b>, liquid <b>Pathos</b> and powdered <b>Angst</b> all can be copied into material substances since the composition is the point in them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Spirit 3 \u2013 Converting Ephemera</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Stepping Sideways</b> converts your body and, at a higher <b>Difficulty</b>, your equipment to <b>Ephemera</b> while transposing the <i>Gauntlet</i>. You can simply reverse the effect when coming back and bring <b>Ephemeral</b> objects with you.<br /> <br /> They will convert into <b>Matter</b>. But not into any <b>Matter</b>. Just as your <b>Ephemeral</b> body retains its physical properties adapted to <i>Umbral</i> places you visit, the object will retain its otherworldly composition in a <b>Material</b> version, likely one that adapts to <i>Reality Zones</i>.<br /> <br /> It's more unpredictable than the previous rote, but it is also more faithful. Now it is the original completely, and you can bring the Rembrandt or the book without loss. Even the strangest properties are likely to translate, even if altered, and enchantments too. <b>Tass</b> is very likely to be just as powerful and keep <b>Resonance</b>, though the adaptation may change how you can use it.<br /> <br /> Adding <u><b>Matter 2</b></u> gives you finer control over the substance of the translation. You can make sure it will remain as faithful as possible, or the opposite, change it on purpose for whatever goal you have in mind. <u><b>Matter 3</b></u> gives you finer control over form, which can be used to hide its nature or create a protective layer.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Prime 2</b></u> in the original example from the book is just bloat, but you can add to legitimately get more out of it, either extra mass without taking from the local <i>Penumbra</i> or some protection over exceptional properties like enchantments and <b>Charms</b>.<br /> <br /> On one hand, this effect is temporary. You have to put successes towards <b>Duration</b> or the item will eventually turn back into pure <b>Ephemera</b>. It won't instantly dematerialize, though, it's likely that it'll be as if it just crossed, and you can reinforce the effect to keep it around. In fact, it's probable that at this point a spell to make it stay will need only <b>Duration</b>, so it isn't as much of a hurdle as it seems.<br /> <br /> Best of all, while <b>Stepping Sideways</b> is <b>Vulgar</b>, the item itself isn't <b>Magic</b>. Unless your <b>Effect</b> changes it to be something too bizarre, what the item was before is just its nature. The <b>Magic</b> to keep it anchored is also <b>Coincidental</b>, as you're not doing anything weird, just ensuring it will stay real like expected of any object.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Here, the bottom line</b></u> is that you're fully bringing your target. <b>Reality</b> can change it, but won't undo it or merely normalize it. Well, usually. Add <b>Spheres</b> to exert control over the result.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>EXAMPLE</b></i></u><br /> <br /> Now the <b>Mage</b> can do exactly what you wanted and bring the swords, all of them. Since some are &quot;just&quot; inhumanly good craftsmanship and the material property of imprinting defiance against a substance, they'll likely translate well, but the details may change. Adding <u><b>Matter</b></u> is enough to ensure they keep working perfectly well.<br /> <br /> Two of the swords are special, though, even for their peers. The <b>Mage</b> doesn't know, but will find out when their powers \u2013 if in an altered expression \u2013 manifest. One was enchanted for a <b>Djinn Sultan</b> when made eons ago, while the other accrued strange magics through the life of its original, bloodthirsty owner.<br /> <br /> After that the rest is <b>maintenance</b>. Since the item is already in the <i>Material</i> and its existence isn't by <b>Magic</b>, the upkeep ritual just prolongs the stay of something otherwise natural, even if super. All successes go to <b>Duration</b>, and if the <b>Mage</b> is careful this will be a 5 rolls ritual of <b>Coincidental Magic</b> at <b>Difficulty 3</b> with 3 dice. Aim at a <b>Month</b> long <b>Duration</b> (3/4 successes) and you're gold, just renew every 3 weeks for safety. You can probably do better, but no need to try your luck. At higher <b>Arete</b> it'll be trivial to make it <b>indefinite</b> and renew every couple years.<br /> <br /> If the <b>Mage</b> wants, they can add <b>Prime</b> even in the dark to protect hitherto unknown abilities. It isn't reliable without knowing what to protect and will raise the target successes, but doable it is, and better than nothing. Won't affect the <b>Maintenance</b> ritual anyway.<br /> <br /> You can bring anything at this point. Higher levels will give you fidelity, ease and scale, but as long as you can hold something, you can bring it with <u><b>Spirit 3</b></u>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Spirit 4 \u2013 Rend Gauntlet and Bind Fetish</b></u><br /> <br /> First of all: forget <u><b>Prime</b></u>. This is not <u><b>Prime</b></u> and <u><b>Prime</b></u> is not this. You can't just copy a <b>Wonder</b> and it being <b>Ephemeral</b> won't change this. I can say, though, that using <u><b>Spirit 3</b></u> to build it with <b>Ephemera</b> would be rad as hell, but would still follow the regular creation rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Rending the <i>Gauntlet</i></b> gives you a more direct and scalable means to bring objects. Instead of traversing with just a few at a time like drug trafficking, you can open a portal and dump <i>Umbral</i> contraband to your heart's content. Fill trucks with otherworldly stuff.<br /> <br /> Go wild. Find the <i>Spire Realm</i> where the Library of Alexandria is standing, but filled with sports almanacs and collectible cards from all eras and places, turn the floor into a portal and let gravity do the work. It's worth it just to see the obscene earnings of those chariot racers from Rome and Constantinople adjusted to today's dollar (it's shocking).<br /> <br /> Since you're not translating anything to <b>Matter</b>, the items are more likely to retain their original properties, but any change is also more wild. You'll need to start <b>Maintenance</b> right away, but with more dice and some other <b>Spheres</b> you can at least prepare the warehouse and trucks instead, which is easier, or try the effect as an <b>area</b> if the <b>ST</b> allows. <b>Maintenance</b> is still <u><b>Spirit 3</b></u>, so same <b>Diff</b>.<br /> <br /> Adding <u><b>Matter</b></u> and <u><b>Prime</b></u> still has the same effects, but is less relevant if you don't want to change the items. The portal is obviously <b>Vulgar</b> and probably very hard to hide, but the item just is, <b>Sleepers</b> be damned.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bottom line</b></u>, <u><b>Spirit 4</b></u> scales and simplifies. If 3 gives you exactly what you want, 4 makes it a trivial thing.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>EXAMPLE</b></i></u><br /> <br /> Why bring only a few swords? The <b>Mage</b> prepares the <b>Sanctum</b>'s armory to house spirits in the <i>Material</i> for a year, then opens a portal. If they have enough <u><b>Correspondence</b></u> and/or successes, the cabal just enters the city and take anything that isn't stuck to the ground and even some things that are. Whole walls will be used to expand the <b>Chantry</b>, and one <b>Mage</b> is explaining to the others that the Adamantine door of the vault is worth more money than any treasure they may have left behind.<br /> <br /> Sure, the new building will need <b>maintenance</b> with <b>Magic</b> until <i>local reality</i> sets in but is more than worth it.<br /> <br /> <b>Fetishes</b> are their own thing and require other considerations. It won't just bring the item to the <i>Material</i> or replicate its properties, but do something else entirely. A <b>Fetish</b> takes a spirit, one that must be awaken and aware, puts it literally inside a material object, and derives its power from the <b>symbolism</b> of the spirit, not its powers. The creator has some influence on the final result, but so does the spirit and the circumstances, no one individually fine control what the result will do.<br /> <br /> So with <b>Binding</b> you'll play a very peculiar game with the original item. <b>Arousing</b> it is the best starting point, although it may fail as it isn't the spirit of an object, it's an object that's made of spirit stuff. Working or not, isn't as if something can stop you from putting inanimate <b>Ephemera</b> into inanimate <b>Matter</b>.<br /> <br /> While you do it you state more or less what you think should happen, that's a primary guideline. The power of the spirit defines if what you asked for is within reach, and scale down or up by itself after initial input. The spirit &quot;states&quot; its own wants, and that modifies the result either blessing it, giving more powers, or cursing the item, although inanimate <b>Ephemera</b> probably doesn't have a big wish list. The <b>ST</b> adds more weirdness as they see fit (in your case is you). Ignore the actual properties of the item and focus on story and significance, unless you feel like using those powers.<br /> <br /> Long term, though, <b>Fetishes</b> have a mind of their own that will learn and change with their experiences. With time the <b>Ephemeral</b> item within will acquire a consciousness of sorts because that's what full blown spirits do, like those bound into <b>Fetishes</b>. That changes the desires of the spirit and the circumstances, and the powers of the <b>Fetish</b> follow suit.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bottom line</b></u>, you'll create a <b>Fetish</b>, but that's a lot easier than regular <b>Wonders</b> of same power level and the item is unlikely to offer any resistance even if it's powerful enough to be worth using it in lieu of a proper spirit. But it will be a <b>Fetish</b> and will get weird with time<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>EXAMPLE</b></i></u><br /> <br /> One of the swords has preternatural ease cutting... Paper. I mean, it is a cool trick at parties and all, the paper barely touches it, but not going to win the day. Or is it?<br /> <br /> The <b>Mage</b> decides to bind it into a small paper cutter blade knife. Since it's still an exceptional sword, it should be able to cut like it even in the humble body of a paper cutter blade. And since it cuts the archetypal medium of written words, they should have the power of metaphorically cutting short words, shouldn't it?<br /> <br /> Since the <b>Mage</b> doesn't know what such an old spirit will be like if roused, they <b>bind</b> it <b>dormant</b>, as an object. All the rules for creating <b>Fetishes</b> are followed, the cutter is small but beautifully made and intricate, the <b>binding</b> is a success. It is now that the <b>ST</b> takes everything and create the actual properties.<br /> <br /> It is indeed an exceptional spirit even if not the most magical of the bunch. If <b>roused</b>, it would be thousands of years old and a sword that no <b>Garou king</b> would be shy of claiming even in its infancy, it saw the history of the abandoned city and knew its inhabitants before humans had learned to write (again). It would be worth the few but solid powers attributed. Or rather, it is, because you can't go through all nine yards of making a <b>Fetish</b> with such potential without considerable risk of it <b>awakening</b> as at least a <b>Lesser Jagling</b>.<br /> <br /> Now that the power is established, the <b>ST</b> decides this small, concealable knife packs the full punch of a <u><b>+6 damage</b></u> sword that <u><b>doubles successes in a 10</b></u> for both <b>attack</b> and <b>damage</b>, as long as it's used as if it was a <b>saber</b>. It also <b>cuts words</b> by <b>silencing</b> people with a subtle move that can be hidden or pretended as just cutting paper (that it cuts only as well as a very keen and well kept paper cutter blade). Victims can <b>resist</b> with <u><b>Willpower against Gnosis 7</b></u>, so good luck for most, <u><b>failure is mutism for a day and a night</b></u>.<br /> <br /> As the spirit <b>awoke</b>, it can also choose its share of effects. Since it was abandoned by its long time people when they vanished from the city, it wants to never be left behind again, and to be properly cared for. Small as it is, it will be with the <b>Mage</b> all the time no matter what they do about it, the knife just <b>teleports</b> to pockets and won't change <b>owner</b> easily. It also <u><b>cuts the words</b></u> of the <b>user</b> when it feels <u><b>neglected for a whole day</b></u>.<br /> <br /> Finally, it feels its &quot;<b>family</b>&quot;, be the other swords, the owner or previous owners (the <b>Djinni</b>). It <u><b>changes temperature</b></u> kinda <u><b>randomly when any of those is nearby</b></u>, regardless if the spirit knows why or what it thinks of them. If used as part of a <b>ritual</b> to do <b>Staying Maintenance</b> on a sword of the <b>family</b>, it helps the <b>ritual</b> as other participant with its <u><b>Gnosis 7</b></u>.<br /> <br /> Everything the sword <b>means</b> was used for the item, while actual form and material properties are only tangentially considered, because what empowers the <b>Fetish</b> isn't the magic in it, but its role as an <b>entity</b> with an <b>identity</b>, a <b>history</b>, a <b>web of relationships</b> and <b>meanings</b> and a <b>place to inhabit</b> in the <i>cosmos</i>. A powerful <b>Wonder</b> is probably a bad candidate for this process as it is stronger by itself, but that Rembrandt can be a solid choice without any power at all.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Spirit 5 \u2013 Create Ephemera</b></u><br /> <br /> I said before that sometimes <b>Ephemera</b> just work in a sufficiently compatible way with the <i>Material</i> that it'll sticks for longer, even forever in the <i>Material</i>.<br /> <br /> With <u><b>Spirit 5</b></u> you just make it. Instead of using whatever <b>Ephemera</b> is at hand, you make your own with strippers and blackjack. You change the very <b>Ephemera</b> the item is made of, and with a few more successes it is <b>Lasting</b>: not a <b>permanent spell</b>, but an effect that isn't a <b>spell</b> anymore once done. The game is unclear when we can make those at lower ranks, but<u><b> 5 </b></u>is the sure thing.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bottom line</b></u>, <u><b>Spirit 5</b></u> just bulldoze all questions and do the deed. You take the item, decide how it works put it in the <i>Material</i> the way you want and it will stay until removed as anything else in the <i>Material</i> if this is what you want.<br /> <br /> You can even make it <b>anchor</b> to your person, so if it is ever <b>destroyed</b>, as a spirit it will <b>reform</b> close to you, period, and the <b>reform</b> won't cause <b>Paradox</b> because it isn't <b>Magic</b>, it's just a spirit doing what a spirit does.<br /> <br /> The one thing <u><b>Spirit</b></u> won't do alone even at<u><b> 5 </b></u>is prevent changes to magical powers or sources of energy like <b>Essence</b>, as this is the purview of <u><b>Prime</b></u> and other <b>Spheres</b>.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>EXAMPLE</b></i></u><br /> <br /> Upon reaching <u><b>Spirit 5</b></u> the <b>Mage</b> decided to get rid of yearly <b>maintenance</b> and put everything they learned about the swords to use.<br /> <br /> They set apart the <b>Fetish</b> one and prepare the others. The two magical ones will need careful work to not risk their spells. The other swords, at this point they saw what each could do, can do now, how they changed or not, how other things changed or not, they saw virtually every possible iteration of <b>Ephemera</b> conceivable, lots of inconceivable ones, and theorized new iterations entirely.<br /> <br /> So they gather all those swords, decides on the experiments they can execute, develop a huge <b>ritual</b> to anchor them all in the <i>Material</i> and in a week or so they're all permanently tied to this <i>Realm</i>. It could be sooner, but the <b>ritual</b> also do a lot of changes to each one in accordance with the <b>Mage's</b> specifications.<br /> <br /> Changes that almost immediately aren't what they really want anymore, so if no one takes the <b>Master of Spirit</b> out of the lab they'll go for years tweaking the sword collection either for curiosity or whim.<br /> <br /> <br /> What must be clear is that &quot;<b>permanent</b>&quot; has a very specific meaning in <b>Mage</b>. Or rather, two ambiguous meanings the game never clarified. You can have an actual sword for your whole life and pass it down for generations. But it isn't eternal, it isn't unbreakable, and if you want &quot;can&quot; to become &quot;did&quot; you'll have to learn how to do <b>maintenance</b>, oil it regularly with the proper options, get intimate with several pieces, and tools to keep those pieces.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you can have magical things in the game, but that doesn't mean &quot;<b>permanent</b>&quot; unless it is &quot;<b>permanent</b>&quot;, which is a <u><i><b>stupidly high bar</b></i></u> as it either means the ongoing <b>spell</b> never ends if not subject to an exceptionally powerful and possibly tailored <b>dispel effect</b>, or it means the <b>effect</b> ceases to be a <b>spell</b> at all and is just <b>reality</b>, undeniable <b>reality</b>.<br /> <br /> You don't need <u><b>Spirit 5</b></u>, because &quot;<b>Permanent</b>&quot; is overkill. <u><b>Spirit 1</b></u> sufices to appreciate a trophy room in the local <i>Penumbra</i> with mementos you can later take from the wall if you get there again.<b><u> 2 </u></b>to<u><b> 4 </b></u>give you plenty of ways to use the things you brought potentially forever. Most of the really important <b>effects</b> for the &quot;stick&quot; part are simple, <b>Coincidental</b> and low in <b>successes</b>, they can literally be the regular <b>maintenance</b> an item would require anyway, not to say that the place or container itself can take care of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Several minor formatting and a bunch of typos 08-16-2026, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T07:42:41-07:00","id":1563172,"title":"","content":"I largely agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> on her breakdown of the different possibilities, with one caveat.<br /> <br /> I think the Short-Lived Ephemeral Object line in M20 isn\u2019t about crafting a material object out of ephemera, I think it is creating a material object out of thin air and converting it to ephemera. Normally creating ephemera is Spirit 5, but creating matter is only Matter 2/Prime 2 and converting it is only Spirit 3. It\u2019s a clever workaround to accomplish a specific effect with lower sphere ranks so Prime and Matter aren\u2019t bloat, but they are there for a very specific purpose that we aren\u2019t trying to accomplish here.<br /> <br /> Matter 2 and 3 to adjust the translation to something more fitting or stronger is a good optional addition I hadn\u2019t considered before. I like that a lot and the more I think of how the ephemeral presents itself the more I see uses in the conversion process.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do think there\u2019s some utility in the original Consecration idea. I don\u2019t see why a mage couldn\u2019t consecrate an ephemeral object to himself while he himself is ephemeral. It might even work while he is physical. On a technical note, Consecration doesn\u2019t actually shift the object, it makes it enough a part of the mage\u2019s pattern/identity that it shifts when he does. The actual spell doing the transformation is whatever spell is transforming the mage.<br /> <br /> In most cases the mage could accomplish the same thing just by picking up the object and bringing it back across the gauntlet with him. There are only two things consecration brings to the table: 1) it can arguably bypass the size limit on Spirit 2 gauntlet crossing, so it works on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T10:11:47-07:00","id":1563178,"title":"","content":"First of all, thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> for the very detailed explainer, that is incredibly helpful.<br /> <br /> I actually don't have much to contribute after that, it pretty much answers all my questions. I'm very ok with some maintainance requirements that extend the 'shelf life' of Ephemeral items, and hadn't even considered storing them in the penumbra. There's probably a Time effect that can slow degradation, too.<br /> And as a side note, the fluff in your examples made for a very entertaining read.<br /> <br /> I also looked up some abilities of Spirits and Wraiths that could play into it; Wraiths have a (very high end) Flux art to return Relics to the Skinlands, and Usury can 'imbue' special attributes into items in the Skinlands. Spirits routinely affect the Material with their Charms, so I don't think it's too much of a stretch to think they could manifest an item instead of themselves - as long as it fits with their domain.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>: I think your post unfortunately got cut off, at least it appears to me like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T10:20:40-07:00","id":1563179,"title":"","content":"Well it was supposed to say:<br /> <br /> In most cases the mage could accomplish the same thing just by picking up the object and bringing it back across the gauntlet with him. There are only two things Consecration brings to the table: 1) it can arguably bypass the size limit on Spirit 3 gauntlet crossing, so it works on things the mage can\u2019t pick up. 2) the object doesn\u2019t have to be in the mage\u2019s possession so a clever mage could convert things he doesn\u2019t want to be caught crossing the gauntlet with. Both of these are fairly niche, but I can see them coming up in games where the players don\u2019t have Spirit 3 themselves but have to barter with some other mage to cast it for them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T15:33:18-07:00","id":1563198,"title":"","content":"I always interpreted the Create Object with Ephemera effect to be an alternative to Prime rather than to Spirit 5. It makes a lot of sense as both, though, as Spirit 3 already let you shape Ephemera into an object and then Matter converts it. More dots than Prime 2, but accomplished with another Sphere, though I guess it can be done with Forces, too.<br /> <br /> Consecration was more &quot;another topic&quot; than &quot;not useful&quot;, and I'd add a third use: bypass the Difficulty modifier to Stepping Sideways. Since it's now and &quot;extension&quot; of your Pattern, you're not required to increase successes and Diff to bring those particular items.<br /> <br /> Abd yes, one of the things with Mage is that no power is meant to exist independently. Instead you'll be mixing rules all the time once you get used to it. So, don't have an effect to keep that item in the Material?<br /> <br /> - Your Sanctum can do that by itself,<br /> - You can ask this from a Mentor, Ally or just pay a Tradition colleague,<br /> - Other entities can do that for you that you summon with other Magic,<br /> - Some weird phenomenon covers that for you,<br /> - There's always a Reality Zone,<br /> - Other Spheres can find their own answers:<br /> -- Store in Sanctum. Get or stow with Correspondence.<br /> -- Extend its time in this world with Time, Entropy, maybe encasing in a consecrated form with Matter + Prime.<br /> -- Store within yourself with a Demesne and/or with some judicious use of Mind. Or Life to be more literal.<br /> -- Let it in the Umbra, but its presence is represented with a construct of Forces, bending light to make it visible and imparting kinetic energy.<br /> - Let your Avatar handle it, some of them are capable of doing this.<br /> - A Wonder with the power of anchoring items from other worlds.<br /> - Get help from some Nightfolk.<br /> - Mix and match, each Sphere isn't just giving you some powers, they're also multiplying the ways you can make all those options work for you.<br /> <br /> Can't summon Spirits yet? Find a map of the local Umbra in the nearest Chapel, pinpoint a passage to the Underworld. Now you can take a radio or cellphone and use Forces 2, Spirit 2 and Correspondence 2 to send a message to any Wraith you know by directing the effect through the route.<br /> <br /> Your players will be creative as they learn and get used to the system, and Mage is the most &quot;the answer is probably 'you can'&quot; game in WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T06:57:08-07:00","id":1563222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1563125-giving-permanence-to-ephemeral-objects?p=1563198#post1563198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always interpreted the Create Object with Ephemera effect to be an alternative to Prime rather than to Spirit 5. It makes a lot of sense as both, though, as Spirit 3 already let you shape Ephemera into an object and then Matter converts it. More dots than Prime 2, but accomplished with another Sphere, though I guess it can be done with Forces, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, Create Object With Ephemera is a good workaround to using Prime. It essentially occupies the same space as making objects out of thoughts from Mind 3. I actually don't see that Spirit 3 has the ability to shape ephemera, that looks like its specifically in Spirit 5. Possibly it was supposed to read that Spirit 3 can handle inert ephemera while Spirit 5 is required for spirits themselves. Either way it doesn't matter to the effect since Spirit 3 can convert the ephemera to matter and as you've already pointed out, the various ranks of Matter can do the rest.<br /> <br /> What I thought you were talking about, though, was this passage:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20, pg 522</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By combining this Rank with Matter 3 and Prime 2, the mage can also create short-lived objects from ephemera; such creations must be constructed <i><b>as if they were material things</b></i>, and they fade away at the end of the Effect\u2019s duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>The emphasis is mine. Given the verbiage, I interpret this to be about making an ephemeral object, not making an object out of ephemera. In the former application, Prime 2 might actually be doing something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1563125-giving-permanence-to-ephemeral-objects?p=1563198#post1563198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consecration was more &quot;another topic&quot; than &quot;not useful&quot;, and I'd add a third use: bypass the Difficulty modifier to Stepping Sideways. Since it's now and &quot;extension&quot; of your Pattern, you're not required to increase successes and Diff to bring those particular items.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I had forgotten about the difficulty modifier. Because Spirit so often maps difficulty to Gauntlet rating I sometimes forget that it has other modifiers. Indeed, stepping sideways is one of the rare occasions where going up in sphere rank might lower the difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 08-19-2026, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}